    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d939">

                <pb facs="0975" n="961" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg961"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.6363/547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-15T18:00:00-05:00">April 15, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>387. Minister of State<anchor n="68" xml:id="d939-f1"/> advised me that Mexican
                    tanker has unloaded 161,000 gallons gas oil in Habana for Cumex and urgently
                    requests that it be considered <hi rendition="#italic">ex quota</hi>. I stated I
                    would be glad to cable Washington which would have to make the decision but
                    situation <pb facs="0976" n="962" xml:id="pg962"/> was such that in all
                    frankness I was not at all sanguine that his request could be granted.</p>
                <p>I can see no justification for increasing Cuba’s supply of petroleum products. If
                    Cuban Government were to follow up, its proposal for trade of gasoline for gas
                    oil reported in Embassy’s despatch number 5729 of January 18, 1944,<anchor
                        n="70" xml:id="d939-f2"/> it is believed that all Cuba’s essential
                    requirements could be met. I consequently recommend that this shipment not be
                    considered <hi rendition="#italic">ex quota</hi>. Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d939-f1" n="68" xml:id="d939-f1-content">
                <p>Jorge Mañach y Roberto.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d939-f2" n="70" xml:id="d939-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; the proposal called for a reduction in imports of 6 million gallons
                    of gasoline (to be offset in part by additional supplies of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">carburante</hi> for local Cuban alcohol production) and
                    the import instead of 6 million gallons of gas oil (837.6363/519).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
